Hi Jemma,&nbsp;Thanks for reviewing the other email for me earlier today – much appreciated. Please see the email chain below. Are you able to review the draft reply below too please?&nbsp;Hi Michael,&nbsp;Thank you for your emails and for outlining your concerns regarding Occupational Sick Pay (OSP). I can confirm the firm’s position regarding Occupational Sick Pay (OSP) as follows:&nbsp;Your contract makes it clear that any entitlement to pay during absence is subject to the firm’s sickness policy. That policy is not contractual, and we are not obliged to individually notify employees of its content. Employees are expected to review policies, which are made available from time to time on HiBob. The applicable policy, in place prior to your resignation and your current period of sick leave, governs any entitlement to OSP and SSP.The sickness policy uploaded on 17 November 2025 at 09:59:39 was the first formal iteration of a written sickness policy. No previous written sickness policy was in place.Condition 7(5) relating to OSP was included in this first iteration. The policy was published to clarify eligibility for occupational sick pay going forward.The firm confirms that no employee currently working their notice is in receipt of OSP under the terms of the policy.&nbsp;In line with this, the firm maintains that you are not eligible for OSP during your notice period and any entitlement is limited to Statutory Sick Pay (SSP).&nbsp;Kind regards,Natasha &nbsp;&nbsp;From: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt; Sent: 10 December 2025 15:03To: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: M Burke&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Natasha,&nbsp;I am sorry to chase again, but time is fast running out if I am to return to work, against medical advice, in order to receive full pay. The lack of response is potentially prejudicing my ability to mitigate my loss.&nbsp;&nbsp;If you can also please clarify the company's position on my unilateral contract change that would be helpful.&nbsp;Similarly, can you confirm the position re the courier who is due to arrive on Friday?&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Sent: Tuesday, December 9, 2025 5:43:13 PMTo: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: M Burke &nbsp;Hi Natasha,&nbsp;Could you come back to me on the below at your earliest opportunity or let me know when you will be able to respond?&nbsp;&nbsp;As advised before, this is quite pressing.&nbsp;Given that we are now on day 7 of my absence (meaning the firm's position as I understand it is that I am only entitled to SSP for those 7 days as opposed to OSP), if the firm maintain that position then I will be forced to consider what options are open to me to dispute those 7 days, and any further that I assert should be paid at OSP and not SSP.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Sent: Monday, December 8, 2025 7:13:08 PMTo: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: M Burke &nbsp;Hi Natasha,&nbsp;Thank you for this and for that information.&nbsp;Bearing all of this in mind i.e. that the policy has been changed without notification, that the policy constitutes (as you have termed it) part of my contractual framework, and that the policy makes a material change to my contractual position, is it still the firm's position that I am not eligible for OSP?&nbsp;&nbsp;I note that the firm, as is any employer, is obliged to notify their employees of any change in their contractual position.&nbsp;Kind regards,Michael&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Monday, December 8, 2025 5:57:34 PMTo: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Subject: RE: M Burke &nbsp;Hi Michael,&nbsp;Thank you for your email and for your patience whilst I responded to your queries.&nbsp;I can confirm the following:&nbsp;Date of issue: The Sickness Absence Policy was formally issued on 17 November 2025.Communication to staff: The policy was made available to all staff on the same date through its upload to HiBob (according to the screenshot attached), which, as you know, is our central repository for HR policies and guidance. No separate email notification was issued at that time.&nbsp;Regarding your request for a previous version of the policy, I can confirm that we did not have a Sickness Absence Policy in place prior to this iteration, so there is no earlier version to provide.&nbsp;Please let me know if you need anything further.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;​​​​Natasha&nbsp;Geraldo&nbsp;BairdHead&nbsp;of&nbsp;HR+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;643This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt; Sent: 08 December 2025 16:36To: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: M Burke&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Natasha,&nbsp;I hope you had a nice weekend.&nbsp;Further to the below, can you let me know when you will be in a position to respond?&nbsp;&nbsp;As previously advised, the loss of two weeks full pay is not trivial. If it is the company's position that it has appropriately and clearly advised me of a change to what you have termed the contractual framework, then I will need to consider going against the clear medical advice I have been provided and returning to work sooner than I have been advised.&nbsp;&nbsp;On the company's current stance, I am already at a loss of 6 days full pay and the longer this situation exists, the more at a detriment I will be.&nbsp;If you can let me know as soon as possible that would be appreciated.&nbsp;Kind regards,Michael&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Sent: Friday, December 5, 2025 6:16:41 PMTo: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: M Burke &nbsp;Hi Natasha,&nbsp;Thank you for responding, and on your non-working day.&nbsp;&nbsp;I am sure as you will appreciate I am keep to resolve this as quickly as possible, especially in light of it becoming new information to me that the company is stating I am not eligible for OSP when I was anticipating that I would be. Two weeks full pay is not a trivial sum of money.&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Friday, December 5, 2025 6:04:01 PMTo: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Subject: RE: M Burke &nbsp;Hi Michael,&nbsp;Thank you for your email. I will respond on Monday. &nbsp;Kind regards,​​​​Natasha&nbsp;Geraldo&nbsp;BairdHead&nbsp;of&nbsp;HR+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;643This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt; Sent: 05 December 2025 09:27To: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: HR Team &lt;hr@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: M Burke&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Natasha, Colleagues,&nbsp;Thank you for providing this. I note from the cover page that this was issued in November 2025.&nbsp;Can you confirm a) the exact date when it was issued and b) when it was communicated to staff that it had been issued?&nbsp;If you could also provide me with the version of the policy that was in place immediately prior to this iteration of the policy that would be appreciated.&nbsp;Clearly if this iteration has been issued with changes to it, and it is said that this document forms part of an employee's contract, then any changes to it should be notified to the staff to whom it applies as it amounts to a change in contractual terms.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;MichaelFrom: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Thursday, December 4, 2025 10:13:27 PMTo: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Cc: HR Team &lt;hr@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: M Burke &nbsp;Hello Michael,&nbsp;I have seen your email, and I am sharing a copy of the Sickness Absence Policy here for your reference.&nbsp;Please let me know if you need anything else or have any further questions.&nbsp;Kind regards,N &nbsp;​​​​Natasha&nbsp;Geraldo&nbsp;BairdHead&nbsp;of&nbsp;HR+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;643This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt; Sent: 04 December 2025 21:07To: Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; HR Team &lt;hr@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: M Burke&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Dear Colleagues,&nbsp;Having received an out of office from Natasha advising she is out of office until Monday 8 December, and given the urgency to establish the position regarding the Sickness Policy and SSP, I am forwarding this email to the HR inbox.&nbsp;I look forward to hearing from you.&nbsp;Kind regards,Michael&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Thursday, December 4, 2025 9:00 pmTo:&nbsp;Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: M Burke &nbsp;Dear Natasha,&nbsp;Thank you for your email and for providing responses to my queries.&nbsp;&nbsp;Firstly, thank you for confirming that my final pay will include payment for my six days accrued but untaken annual in addition to the pro-rated acting up allowance for the 15 days of employment with the firm in December.&nbsp;Thank you also for confirming the position of the company equipment, it is relieving to hear that as long as the courier collects this on the 12th, there will not be any withheld payment if they do not deliver it by the 15th. Please let me know the details of the courier so I can ensure the equipment is not in use and is ready to be collected.&nbsp;I will attend the office to return the remainder of my equipment (noting some of it remains in the flat in London along with some of my personal items so I need to be in London to deal with that in any event).&nbsp;&nbsp;With regard to the OSP v SSP, thank you for confirming the point regarding the Sickness Policy.&nbsp;&nbsp;I am afraid I do not think I have ever been provided with this. Can you please provide me with this?&nbsp;I also not the firm's position that the policy has been applied consistently. I reserve my position on this for now.&nbsp;Additionally, should I need to return to work, contrary to specific medical advice I.e. the medical document I have provided confirming that I should not be working, on account of being required to, to be eligible for full pay, then I also reserve my position on this.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thank you again for turning this around and for the confirmations provided.&nbsp;&nbsp;I look forward to hearing from you.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for AndroidFrom:&nbsp;Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Thursday, December 4, 2025 8:20:27 PMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: M Burke &nbsp;Dear Michael,&nbsp;Thank you for your email and for the welcome back. I appreciate you keeping us informed about your fitness for work, and I have answered your questions below.&nbsp;Eligibility for Occupational Sick Pay (OSP)Clause 13.4 of your employment contract states that company sick pay is provided “in accordance with the Company’s Sickness Policy.”&nbsp;The Sickness Policy, therefore, forms part of the contractual framework, and its eligibility criteria apply in full. Under the Policy, employees who have given notice of termination of their employment are not eligible for OSP.&nbsp;To address your question about consistency, I can confirm that the firm has consistently applied the current policy. Employees in comparable circumstances, i.e., those where notice has been given, receive SSP rather than OSP.&nbsp;Return to work and IT accessIf you become medically fit to return to work before 15 December, please let me know as soon as possible. In this instance, we would arrange for the IT team to reinstate your system access so that you can resume work and complete the handover required before your final day.&nbsp;Final payYour final pay will include:SSP for the period of certified sickness absencePayment for your six days of accrued but untaken annual leaveAny days on which you return to work and perform duties before 15 December, which will be paid at your normal rate.&nbsp;Regarding the acting-up allowance, this will be included in your final salary, pro-rated to your last day of employment, as you mentioned below.&nbsp;Company equipmentThank you for confirming that 12 December in the afternoon is suitable for the courier collection; I will arrange this accordingly.&nbsp;The temporary withholding of £1,000 is only to ensure the equipment is returned. Provided the courier collects the items on 12 December as arranged, the firm will not withhold the amount due to any delay caused by the courier’s delivery timeline.&nbsp;TELUS HealthI’m glad to hear that you intend to utilise TELUS Health services, and I encourage you to take full advantage of the support available.&nbsp;If you need any more clarification or if your fitness to return changes, please let me know, and we will support you accordingly.&nbsp;Kind regards,Natasha&nbsp;​​​​Natasha&nbsp;Geraldo&nbsp;BairdHead&nbsp;of&nbsp;HR+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;643This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at 53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website. For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;02 December 2025 22:15To:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: M Burke&nbsp;Dear Michael,&nbsp;Thank you for your email. I’ve noted everything you’ve raised and will review the matters carefully. I’ll get back to you as soon as possible with a full response.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;​​​​Natasha&nbsp;Geraldo&nbsp;BairdHead&nbsp;of&nbsp;HR+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;643This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website. For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;02 December 2025 09:40To:&nbsp;Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: M Burke&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Dear Natasha,&nbsp;Welcome back to PG after your maternity leave. I hope you and the family are adjusting well.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thank you for your email. I am disappointed to note the position taken by the company given my relentless +6 years worth of service to the firm and given I remain one of the longest standing employees. I also note that I am hopeful of returning to work prior to 15 December. In the event this is possible, can you please let me know who I should contact and how to have my system access restored?&nbsp;In terms of the eligibility, can you point me to where in my contract it states that to be eligible for full pay (termed OSP in your below email) I have not given notice of termination of my employment? For the avoidance of doubt, it does not stand to reason that simply due to my resignation, that in of itself does not constitute non-compliance with the terms of the Agreement.&nbsp;&nbsp;Further, can you advise if the same eligibility criteria (and the same resultant decision to not permit full pay in exception to 13.4 of my contract) have been applied to other members of staff who have been required to take a period of sickness during their notice period?&nbsp;&nbsp;Regarding my final pay, and in the event I am entitled to receive full pay for my absence (subject to the above), I believe my final pay should consist of:&nbsp;Full pay from 1 December to 12 December (anticipated as full pay under 13.4 of my contract)Any full pay for days which I return to full work;Outstanding annual leave of 6 days; and11 days worth of my acting up allowance (£3,175 gross). The 1 September letter from Raminder confirms that this will be effective from 1 September 2025 and will be reviewed on a monthly basis. It further states that any changes to this will be discussed in advance and confirmed in writing. I have received no such notice and so this is still due paid for this month.&nbsp;&nbsp;In terms of the company equipment:&nbsp;I note my account has been disabled on account of allowing me to focus on my health and recovery, thank you for this. I do note however that this will prevent me from progressing or completing any handover before 15 December. This will constrict the time I am available to complete this in.&nbsp;Thank you for confirming a courier can be arranged. If a courier can be arranged to attend my property on the afternoon of Friday 12 December 2025, I will have the computer screens and spare laptop ready to be collected.Noted regarding the £1,000 being withheld. Can you please confirm that this will not be unreasonably withheld, i.e. in circumstances where the courier has collected the equipment on 12 December, but it is not delivered to Pogust Goodhead by 15 December?&nbsp;Thank you for providing the TELUS information, I will likely avail of this while it is available.&nbsp;&nbsp;I look forward to hearing from you with confirmation of the above.&nbsp;&nbsp;Best wishes,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;01 December 2025 12:48To:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; burke7y@hotmail.com&nbsp;&lt;burke7y@hotmail.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: M Burke&nbsp;Dear Michael,&nbsp;Thank you for your email and for sharing your Statement of Fitness for Work. We have noted the details of your sick leave, and I am sorry to hear you are feeling unwell.&nbsp;In line with your contract of employment and our sickness absence policy, eligibility for occupational sick pay (OSP) requires, among other conditions, that the employee has not given notice of termination of their employment. As you have given notice, you are unfortunately not eligible for OSP during your notice period.&nbsp;Accordingly, your final pay will be calculated as follows:&nbsp;Sick leave during notice period: 12 days will be covered by statutory sick pay (SSP).Outstanding annual leave: 6 days will be paid in your final payslip.&nbsp;Please note the following regarding company equipment and IT access:&nbsp;Your IT account will be disabled for the duration of your sick leave to allow you to focus on your health and recovery.Your attendance at the office is not required whilst you are on sick leave. Please let me know a convenient date and time for the collection of your company equipment, and we will arrange a courier.If the company equipment is not returned by 15 December, £1,000 will be withheld from your final salary until the kit is returned.&nbsp;We would also like to remind you that support is available through our Employee Assistance Programme (EAP) via TELUS Health. I have attached the information for your reference.&nbsp;Thank you again for your contribution to the firm. We wish you well for the future. If you have any questions about your final pay or require clarification, please don’t hesitate to contact me.&nbsp;Kind regards,​​​​Natasha&nbsp;Geraldo&nbsp;BairdHead&nbsp;of&nbsp;HR+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;643This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website. For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;01 December 2025 08:45To:&nbsp;HR Team &lt;hr@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;M Burke&nbsp;Dear colleagues,&nbsp;Please find attached a Statement of Fitness for Work, which verifies that I have not been, and remain not fit for work for the period of 20 November to 15 December 2025. Please note this is password protected (as was provided by my GP) and the password is my date of birth in the following format: DDMMYYYY.&nbsp;&nbsp;I have tried to avoid using this sick note, since it was provided on 20 November by taking holiday, in an attempt to reconcile me being able to return to work, but unfortunately, this has not been possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;Under clause 13.4 of my contract of employment, I am entitled to received up to 10 days company sick pay. The days, commencing from 1 December 2025 run through until 12 December 2025 (inc) fall within this entitlement and should be paid in full. I will endeavour of course to make myself available to return to work prior to 15 December 2025, mindful that I am still contributing to my team, and my clients. I am also mindful of the firm's ask for me to provide a thorough handover. I will endeavour to provide a handover on those matters which I have conduct of as best I can before I depart the firm (Pan-NOx, Ford, Volvo, British Airways, UEFA and easyJet) and will be in the office on 15 December to hold any meetings required.&nbsp;I will also keep myself abreast of any developments on the litigations such that I am fully versed in any material changes in the event I am able to return to work prior to the 15 December 2025.&nbsp;&nbsp;I note that I presently have 6 days remaining of my holiday entitlement for the year. I would be grateful if this accrued holiday is paid to me in my final salary and that this is confirmed by return.&nbsp;&nbsp;As above, if I am able to return to work prior to the 15 December 2025, then I will certainly endeavour to. I am very mindful of my commitments to my team, and to my clients. In the event I am not fit to return to work before 15 December 2025, I will be present in the office on 15 December 2025 to complete my last working day, bid my colleagues farewell, and handover my equipment.&nbsp;Please confirm this by return.&nbsp;&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;Michael​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;"}

